//! Emigration by soft capacity (ADR-0020 section 6, design note of the emigration): in the
//! last second of each year, after its births and deaths, each household with a member of
//! 18 or more leaves whole with the chance `e = min(0.5, P / K − 1)` while the living
//! exceed the capacity `K`.
//!
//! The expected values come from `tools/state_reference.py` (scenario "emigration"), which
//! runs the model of `tools/world_reference.py`, written from the design note and not from
//! this code.
//!
//! Scenario "emigration": seed 0xff, founder tag `test:emigration33`, the switch off, the
//! capacity 14, 22 years, on the test data of "clan" with practically no deaths (accident
//! 1e-9), the fertility window from 16 to 45 and no separation. Three couples (sims 1 and 2,
//! 3 and 4, 5 and 6, the women 16 to 16.5) and two children alone in households of their
//! own (sim 7, a boy of 10, and sim 8, a girl of 8). At the end of year 2 (`P` 16,
//! `e` = 1/7) household 1 leaves with its dependent children, household 3 with sim 5
//! pregnant; the two children alone draw nothing and stay. In year 14 sim 8 (23) leaves
//! alone. At the end of year 20 (`P` 19) household 2 leaves with sim 3 pregnant and
//! sixteen children; sim 14, moved out at 18, draws on her own and stays.

